The hook run directly, outside `playbook-transition` (which captures the stderr of a hook that
exits 0): with `BOOPING_BIN` pointing at a command that exits 1, it exits 0 and stderr carries the
warning. The script is the plugin's own copy, located through the root `booping` resolves for its
core playbooks.

-- fixtures/cwd/fake-booping --
#!/bin/sh
exit 1
-- cmd --
chmod +x fake-booping
env BOOPING_ARTIFACT=plans/p/index.md BOOPING_BIN=./fake-booping sh -c "exec \"$(python -c 'from booping.rendering import get_plugin_root; print(get_plugin_root())')/playbooks/_scripts/open-items-follow-plan\" open"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
warning: open-items follow-plan failed (exit 1)
